{"page": 5, "kind": "cell", "table": 1, "row": 10, "col": 4, "x": null, "text": "• French: subject to king, traders, missionaries, Catholic, built relationships with Native Americans • Spanish: subject to king, traders, soldiers and missionaries, Catholic, wanted to convert Native Americans, incorporated Native American laborers • English: established local government, settlers, farmers and indentured servants, non-Catholics, wanted a purely settler society, migration pressures • Dutch: charters, trade agreements with Native Americans, fur traders, explorers, Mennonites, Dutch Reformed Church", "id": "u100", "furniture": false}
