{"page": 8, "kind": "cell", "table": 1, "row": 14, "col": 3, "x": null, "text": "Content Standard SS.5.6.7.2 Explain how principles in the Declaration of Independence became unifying ideas of American democracy", "id": "u195", "furniture": false}
{"page": 8, "kind": "cell", "table": 1, "row": 14, "col": 4, "x": null, "text": "• Principles of Declaration: ‘all men are created equal’, ‘inalienable rights’, ‘government deriving their just powers from the consent of the governed’, ‘right of the people to alter or to abolish it’ • Ideas of American Democracy: challenge an unjust government, life, liberty, pursuit of happiness, no kings, popular sovereignty", "id": "u196", "furniture": false}
